# Devoted Druid: "{T}: Add {G}." and "Put a -1/-1 counter on this creature: Untap this creature." The counter is a cost (CR
# 602.2b), so the first untap leaves a 0/1 with one counter that taps for a second {G}; the second untap's counter makes it
# 0/0, and it dies (CR 704.5f) before the untap resolves, the ruling's case. Bot1 casts it on turn 1 off Forest and Mox
# Emerald and, on turn 3 (no longer summoning sick), taps it, untaps it, taps it again and untaps it a second time. The
# counter is on it while the first untap is still on the stack, and the second's has killed it before Bot1 gets priority.

